  "content": {
    "title": "Masters tee times 2026: Saturday pairings, third round groups, TV schedule",
    "text": "April 10, 2026Updated April 11, 2026, 12:51 p.m. ETIt's on to the weekend at Augusta National Golf Club.Following the first 36 holes at the 2026 Masters Tournament, reigning champion Rory McIlroy looks to be on the path to winning back-to-back green jackets with a score of 12-under par in the tournament. McIlroy ended Friday's second round with a run of birdies in his final four holes to give him 7-under par on the day.Sam Burns will be in the grouping with McIlroy on the weekend, as Burns and Patrick Reed both sit in a tie for second place at 6-under par 144. Two-time Masters champion Scottie Scheffler is tied for 24th place on the leaderboard at even par after a roller coaster Friday.There remain 36 holes left to be played during the next two days at Augusta, with the culminating event being the receiving of the green jacket inside Butler Cabin late Sunday afternoon. McIlroy will be the hunted among the golfers in the field after he set the Masters record for the largest 36-hole lead in the history of the tournament at six strokes.Some notable golfers missed the cut on Friday, with the most notable and surprising being Bryson DeChambeau, who will end his trip to the Masters with a 6-over par score following the first two rounds.Here's a look at Saturday's third round tee times at the 2026 Masters, as well as how to watch all the action at golf's first major of the year:Masters Round 3 tee times, matchupsAll times Eastern9:31 a.m.: Kurt Kitayama and Alex Noren9:42 a.m.: Charl Schwartzel and Rasmus Hojgaard9:53 a.m.: Jon Rahm and Si Woo Kim10:04 a.m.: Brian Harman and Corey Conners10:15 a.m.: Sergio Garcia and Maverick McNealy10:26 a.m.: Keegan Bradley and Viktor Hovland10:37 a.m.: Justin Thomas and Gary Woodland10:48 a.m.: Samuel Stevens and Adam Scott11:10 a.m.: Marco Penge and Matt McCarty11:21 a.m.: Jordan Spieth and Sepp Straka11:32 a.m.: Aaron Rai and Jacob Bridgeman11:43 a.m.: Patrick Cantlay and Sungjae Im11:54 a.m.: Dustin Johnson and Russell Henley12:05 p.m.: Harris English and Ryan Gerard12:16 p.m.: Ludvig Aberg and Scottie Scheffler12:38 p.m.: Collin Morikawa and Brian Campbell12:49 p.m.: Nick Taylor and Matt Fitzpatrick1 p.m.: Hideki Matsuyama and Michael Brennan1:11 p.m.: Jake Knapp and Xander Schauffele1:22 p.m.: Ben Griffin and Max Homa1:33 p.m.: Chris Gotterup and Brooks Koepka1:55 p.m.: Jason Day and Cameron Young2:06 p.m.: Haotong Li and Kristoffer Reitan2:17 p.m.: Wyndham Clark and Tyrrell Hatton2:28 p.m.: Shane Lowry and Tommy Fleetwood2:39 p.m.: Patrick Reed and Justin Rose2:50 p.m.: Rory McIlroy and Sam BurnsMasters Leaderboard 2026Here's an updated look at the leaderboard for the 2026 Masters Tournament following Friday's second round at Augusta National:1. Rory McIlroy: -12T2. Patrick Reed: -6T2. Sam Burns: -6T4. Tommy Fleetwood: -5T4. Justin Rose: -5T4. Shane Lowry: -5You can get the complete leaderboard here.How to watch Masters Round 3: TV channel, streaming optionsTV channel: CBSStreaming options:Paramount+ | Masters.com | Masters AppCBS will handle the main feed for the Masters throughout Saturday's third round. The first two hours of coverage on Saturday will air exclusively on Paramount+, before the network takes over for the remainder of each round.Masters.com and the Masters App are other streaming options.Our editors independently choose our recommendations. Some content is produced with paid support from a third party, however our editorial decisions remain independent. If you buy through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices and availability may change.",
